{
  "source": "Smooth-model wind-tunnel data for NACA sections. NACA 0006, 2412, 4412: Abbott, von Doenhoff & Stivers, 'Summary of Airfoil Data', NACA Report 824 (1945), Appendix V figure pages (the same charts as Abbott & von Doenhoff, Theory of Wing Sections, Appendix IV), digitised for this project from the NTRS scan https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19930090976/downloads/19930090976.pdf (axes calibrated on the printed grid; accuracy about +-0.02 cl_max, +-0.5 deg stall angle, +-0.0002 cd, +-0.003/deg a0, +-0.2 deg alpha_L0, +-0.005 cm). NACA 0012: Ladson, NASA TM-4074 (1988), printed Table I (M = 0.15, free transition), https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19880019495/downloads/19880019495.pdf, and Loftin & Cohen, NACA TN 1591 (1948), Fig. 15 (the 0012 data used by Abbott & von Doenhoff, figure), https://ntrs.nasa.gov/api/citations/19930082240/downloads/19930082240.pdf. Report 824 has no NACA 0012 chart.",
  "notes": [
    "Report 824 test Reynolds numbers for 2412 are 3.1, 5.7 and 8.9 million; the model is evaluated at the tabulated Reynolds number.",
    "Lift slope, zero-lift angle and cm_c/4 were fitted over all Reynolds numbers on a chart, so they are listed once per section.",
    "Ladson 0012 cl_max at Re 3.94e6 and 8.86e6 is not used: the angle steps miss the peak (1.484 at 15.1 deg and 1.693 at 18.4 deg are lower bounds).",
    "NACA 2412 measured a0 of 0.100/deg is lower than the 0.104-0.108 of the other sections on the same report; it is what the chart shows.",
    "Standard roughness (not compared): cl_max 0012 1.05 (TN 1591) / 1.22 (Ladson grit, Re 6e6), 2412 1.19, 4412 1.39; cd_min about 0.0090-0.0100.",
    "NACA 64-006 (Report 824 p.177): a0 0.1085, cl_max about 0.84 at 9-10 deg, cd_min 0.0039-0.0040. Not compared: the app only builds NACA 4-digit sections."
  ],
